(Penguin fact card) '
(Penguins are birds that cannot fly. Their wings are stiff flippers that help them swim.) '
(The emperor penguin is the biggest penguin and grows about 1.1 metres tall.) '
(Penguins have thick waterproof feathers. The gentoo penguin can swim at about 35 kilometres per hour.) '
(Penguins eat fish, squid and krill.) '
(Most penguins live in the southern half of the world. The African penguin lives on the coasts of South Africa and Namibia.) '
(Male emperor penguins keep the egg warm on their feet for about 65 days during the Antarctic winter.) '
(Penguins huddle close together to stay warm in freezing wind.) '
ET
